1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.720
[S01] It all started when we really just were very, very young.

2
00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:09.210
[S01] And we were made to wake up way too early in the morning

3
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.140
[S01] to go to some strange place filled with a lot of strangers.

4
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.960
[S01] And to stay there for eight hours,

5
00:00:18.989 --> 00:00:24.559
[S01] to literally be judged and evaluated all day long,

6
00:00:24.589 --> 00:00:27.859
[S01] with even surprise exams and everything.

7
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:31.339
[S01] And after doing that all day, pretty much every day,

8
00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:35.649
[S01] we went, we had to go home and then do homework.

9
00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:41.560
[S01] And I think at some point in this whole process,

10
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:46.359
[S01] we started to feel that reality was disappointing,

11
00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:50.479
[S01] that reality was not what we would like it to be.

12
00:00:50.509 --> 00:00:54.210
[S01] It wasn't fun, it wasn't enjoyable, it wasn't even comfortable.

13
00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:59.119
[S01] And so what we did is, we went inside,

14
00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.380
[S01] into the imagination.

15
00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:05.120
[S01] Because we felt that we always had access to that.

16
00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.040
[S01] We had no control over our lives,

17
00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.840
[S01] we had no control over our schedules,

18
00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.400
[S01] everything that we had to do, what was expected of us

19
00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.040
[S01] and our performance and everything.

20
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.510
[S01] All of that was mandated.

21
00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.890
[S01] But what goes inside of our head, no one could touch that.

22
00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.450
[S01] And we realized that.

23
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.560
[S01] And so during class, in between class,

24
00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.840
[S01] during homework, before and after homework,

25
00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.040
[S01] dreading exams, during all of that,

26
00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:35.120
[S01] we decided that we would, from now on, enhance reality.

27
00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:38.450
[S01] Reality wasn't giving what we were looking for.

28
00:01:39.079 --> 00:01:41.719
[S01] And so we would just go into imaginary worlds

29
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.750
[S01] in which things are much more fun.

30
00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:50.250
[S01] And we can kill time and we can distract ourselves

31
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:56.890
[S01] from this almost grueling, uncomfortable, anxious

32
00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.019
[S01] reality that we were facing day after day,

33
00:02:00.049 --> 00:02:02.280
[S01] without an end in sight, by the way.

34
00:02:03.519 --> 00:02:05.879
[S01] And so we gave up on that, we went inside.

35
00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:11.250
[S01] And school ended and we started to make a living,

36
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.650
[S01] for better or for worse.

37
00:02:13.469 --> 00:02:19.520
[S01] But we never stopped feeling that this world mandates stuff

38
00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.439
[S01] and we just have to follow along,

39
00:02:21.469 --> 00:02:24.020
[S01] we have to do what it does and we have to be judged.

40
00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:27.150
[S01] And by the way, now that we're an adult

41
00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.680
[S01] and we have our own responsibilities,

42
00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.879
[S01] now we have to judge others as well

43
00:02:31.909 --> 00:02:34.120
[S01] and that this is just how the world works.

44
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:39.120
[S01] And so we never stopped feeling that way

45
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.360
[S01] about the present moment.

46
00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:44.439
[S01] We've never stopped feeling that way about reality.

47
00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.460
[S01] And our disagreement with reality has never stopped.

48
00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:52.539
[S01] And therefore, the solution has never changed.

49
00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:54.479
[S01] We're still in our imagination.

50
00:02:55.509 --> 00:02:58.150
[S01] Every time the present moment gets boring

51
00:02:59.449 --> 00:03:01.349
[S01] or uncomfortable

52
00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.050
[S01] or anxious or just overwhelming,

53
00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:10.949
[S01] we escape inside and up into the imagination.

54
00:03:12.979 --> 00:03:14.479
[S01] And we imagine things.

55
00:03:14.509 --> 00:03:19.560
[S01] As children, we perhaps were imagining dinosaurs being real

56
00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.650
[S01] and we're fighting dinosaurs with each other.

57
00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.360
[S01] But now we're doing the same thing.

58
00:03:25.389 --> 00:03:29.259
[S01] We, we listen to a song to escape, first of all.

59
00:03:29.289 --> 00:03:30.919
[S01] But then while that song plays,

60
00:03:30.949 --> 00:03:33.120
[S01] we imagine ourselves as the lead singer,

61
00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.650
[S01] as having that kind of life.

62
00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:41.180
[S01] And it's the same thing, it's escaping into the imagination.

63
00:03:42.979 --> 00:03:46.780
[S01] Whenever we just glaze over, whenever we're looking at,

64
00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.360
[S01] but we're not really looking at anything.

65
00:03:48.389 --> 00:03:51.479
[S01] We're, we're looking at trees and, and really beautiful things,

66
00:03:51.509 --> 00:03:53.539
[S01] but we're not really looking at it.

67
00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:57.400
[S01] There's a different movie playing behind the eyes

68
00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:01.509
[S01] and the attention doesn't even go out to the eyes.

69
00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.340
[S01] She's seeing a dog, that's what's happening.

70
00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:05.780
[S01] Sit.

71
00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.560
[S01] And that's what people do.

72
00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:14.240
[S01] They, at work, in the car, while driving,

73
00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:18.850
[S01] I mean, at any time, whenever reality is just not bearable.

74
00:04:19.379 --> 00:04:22.639
[S01] Or at this point, it's just what we are used to

75
00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.180
[S01] and so that's just what we do.

76
00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:28.750
[S01] And we see people everywhere, just zombie.

77
00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:30.750
[S01] We are the same.

78
00:04:32.709 --> 00:04:34.449
[S01] But now that we're adults,

79
00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:39.920
[S01] now that we do have some kind of end in sight,

80
00:04:39.949 --> 00:04:41.980
[S01] now that we are those adults

81
00:04:42.009 --> 00:04:43.949
[S01] that used to make us do things,

82
00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.810
[S01] with good intentions, of course.

83
00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.879
[S01] Now it is our responsibility

84
00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.639
[S01] and opportunity also

85
00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:56.540
[S01] to finally come out of the imagination

86
00:04:56.569 --> 00:04:59.350
[S01] and to come back into the real world.

87
00:05:01.639 --> 00:05:04.220
[S02] Because this is not working.

88
00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.540
[S02] Every time we escape into the imagination,

89
00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.930
[S02] we don't see anything, we don't hear anything,

90
00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:15.439
[S02] we don't truly think about what we would like to be thinking about.

91
00:05:15.439 --> 00:05:18.379
[S02] And hours pass, days, weeks, months pass.

92
00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.899
[S02] And we think that's just life.

93
00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:26.240
[S02] No, we're deliberately taking our finger off the record button of life.

94
00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:28.939
[S02] Because we don't like it, we don't want to record that.

95
00:05:28.939 --> 00:05:32.060
[S02] We want to, we want to experience what's inside behind the eyes.

96
00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.290
[S02] We want to escape into that.

97
00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:35.899
[S02] And so we take the finger off the record button, we go there.

98
00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.060
[S02] And then we wonder why this, this tape only has

99
00:05:42.079 --> 00:05:46.339
[S02] two hours of every day, if that, twenty minutes of every day recorded.

100
00:05:46.939 --> 00:05:48.170
[S02] And where has the day gone?

101
00:05:48.199 --> 00:05:49.310
[S02] Where has the year gone?

102
00:05:49.339 --> 00:05:51.769
[S02] Where has my youth gone, as people say?

103
00:05:52.279 --> 00:05:53.149
[S02] This is why.

104
00:05:54.769 --> 00:05:58.850
[S02] And it's very understandable to escape into the imagin- imagination like that.

105
00:05:58.850 --> 00:05:59.899
[S02] I don't think it's right.

106
00:06:00.769 --> 00:06:06.560
[S02] The way that we are forced to do things and because I told you so.

107
00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:10.759
[S02] It's not right, but and as parents, perhaps we can think

108
00:06:11.029 --> 00:06:14.949
[S02] how to do it differently and we can do it better, but first we have to come out of it.

109
00:06:16.399 --> 00:06:21.290
[S02] And we see that our imagination is not only a distraction at this point,

110
00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:26.120
[S02] but much worse so, it is actually harassing us.

111
00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.660
[S02] You know exactly what I'm talking about.

112
00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:33.259
[S02] We get those thoughts, whether when we're trying to sleep

113
00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:36.379
[S02] or just randomly throughout the day, that take us somewhere else.

114
00:06:36.649 --> 00:06:39.079
[S02] And it's all imagination, none of it is reality.

115
00:06:39.079 --> 00:06:44.180
[S02] Even if we're trying to, or in our heads think we are preparing something, planning for something.

116
00:06:45.709 --> 00:06:49.129
[S02] You know, putting our time to good use in our, inside of our head.

117
00:06:49.939 --> 00:06:53.240
[S02] There are so many scenarios in there and so many what ifs and so many

118
00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:56.930
[S02] disaster scenarios, by the way,

119
00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:02.990
[S02] that horrify us and they worry us and they harass us and we don't know how to stop it.

120
00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:06.740
[S02] Because this machine has been running for so long

121
00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:08.209
[S02] and it has been

122
00:07:09.199 --> 00:07:11.870
[S02] it running so intensively, right?

123
00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:17.569
[S02] As children imagining dinosaurs and superheroes and things exploding and the ground's lava and all that.

124
00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:22.329
[S02] This machine has really become so trained, so competent.

125
00:07:24.079 --> 00:07:27.829
[S02] But it's been running for so long and it's been running for so, so hard

126
00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:32.329
[S02] that we don't know how to stop it now at this point, even if when we want to stop it.

127
00:07:35.019 --> 00:07:39.740
[S02] And like I said, we can't sleep at night, we, the whole day passes us by.

128
00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:44.060
[S02] And we feel down, we feel anxious, we are worried about things that

129
00:07:44.389 --> 00:07:49.579
[S02] never could possibly occur, but we think they could, or even if they could, they would, most of them don't.

130
00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:54.829
[S02] But we spend all this time and ninety-nine percent imagining

131
00:07:55.189 --> 00:07:58.490
[S02] things that don't need to be imagined, should not be imagined.

132
00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.230
[S02] And we know that.

133
00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:04.819
[S02] We are overwhelmed at this point, not only by reality, but our own imagination.

134
00:08:04.819 --> 00:08:07.610
[S02] We keep bouncing back and forth between one

135
00:08:07.939 --> 00:08:10.310
[S02] thing that overwhelms us and another thing that overwhelms us.

136
00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:14.959
[S02] And we just don't know how to accept this reality that is so overwhelming.

137
00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:20.120
[S02] And we don't know how to stop this imagination, which at this point is so overwhelming.

138
00:08:23.509 --> 00:08:27.319
[S02] And we just have to learn to turn it off at this point.

139
00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:31.939
[S02] And I think how, I think I know how to.

140
00:08:32.539 --> 00:08:35.360
[S02] At least how to make a start, of course, it takes,

141
00:08:36.259 --> 00:08:40.639
[S02] it takes our own doing, someone can't do this for us, but I think I know how to start.

142
00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:47.809
[S02] We're, I do believe that we're fundamentally reasonable people,

143
00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:51.950
[S02] that we're guided by reason, or at least that we have the yearning to be guided by reason.

144
00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.950
[S02] And we just don't know what truly is reasonable.

145
00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.480
[S02] And so I believe that it is only

146
00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:05.990
[S02] false beliefs that make us repeatedly do something that overwhelms us and harasses us.

147
00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.779
[S02] And we allow it, why?

148
00:09:09.529 --> 00:09:11.629
[S02] Because we think it is also good.

149
00:09:12.799 --> 00:09:18.679
[S02] We say, yes, my imagination harasses me, I can't even sleep at night sometimes because of it.

150
00:09:20.059 --> 00:09:23.440
[S02] But if I let go of my imagination,

151
00:09:24.649 --> 00:09:30.529
[S02] I'd be so dull, I'd be, I'd be like a robot, there'd be nothing exciting, nothing interesting about me.

152
00:09:30.919 --> 00:09:35.210
[S02] And by the way, isn't all of beauty, art, you know, music,

153
00:09:36.169 --> 00:09:41.539
[S02] painting, sculpture, everything, doesn't, don't these things come from creativity?

154
00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:43.129
[S02] Aren't artists creative?

155
00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:50.779
[S02] And we say, without imagination, there can be no creativity.

156
00:09:52.019 --> 00:09:55.590
[S03] Surely creativity also comes from that thing which harasses us.

157
00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:57.509
[S03] And so that's the good side of it.

158
00:09:57.539 --> 00:10:00.720
[S03] And if I let go of imagination altogether,

159
00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.639
[S03] sure, I'll be harassed less,

160
00:10:02.669 --> 00:10:05.220
[S03] but I'll never be able to be creative or to find joy in life

161
00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.409
[S03] or to see beauty or to be able to appreciate it.

162
00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:13.409
[S03] This is the false belief that keeps us from this.

163
00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.909
[S03] It's not like we're seeing beauty now.

164
00:10:18.929 --> 00:10:21.600
[S03] It's not like we can even be still enough now

165
00:10:21.629 --> 00:10:23.279
[S03] without our imagination harassing us

166
00:10:23.309 --> 00:10:27.450
[S03] to look at a piece of beauty and to truly appreciate it.

167
00:10:29.129 --> 00:10:31.379
[S03] So clearly, that's not true.

168
00:10:31.399 --> 00:10:34.289
[S03] And I, with reason, with logic,

169
00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:39.960
[S03] I want to disprove that this imagination also has good things about it.

170
00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:43.049
[S03] Because if it doesn't have anything good about it,

171
00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:44.669
[S03] then we can truly let it go.

172
00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.049
[S03] We're only hanging on to it

173
00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.240
[S03] because we think there's something very, very crucial

174
00:10:48.269 --> 00:10:51.029
[S03] to our humanity about it, but there isn't.

175
00:10:53.519 --> 00:10:55.710
[S03] Don't we repeatedly see

176
00:10:56.610 --> 00:11:00.059
[S03] that all kinds of artists, creative makers,

177
00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.519
[S03] designers of any kind?

178
00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.100
[S03] For example, an architect,

179
00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:09.360
[S03] when they see a piece of land perhaps just like this

180
00:11:09.389 --> 00:11:11.399
[S03] and there's nothing built on it yet,

181
00:11:13.049 --> 00:11:14.940
[S03] they look at the landscape, they study it,

182
00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:16.710
[S03] they spend time with it, they are still,

183
00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:18.419
[S03] they are not harassed by their imagination.

184
00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:19.350
[S03] They're fully there.

185
00:11:20.549 --> 00:11:23.519
[S03] And they say, "Aha, I can see it. I can see it.

186
00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.509
[S03] All I have to do now is to draw it,

187
00:11:27.539 --> 00:11:29.730
[S03] you know, write it down and then go build it.

188
00:11:29.759 --> 00:11:31.139
[S03] But I do fully see it."

189
00:11:31.919 --> 00:11:34.919
[S03] And this is not an imagination. This is a vision.

190
00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.210
[S03] Just like our physical vision can see the landscape,

191
00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:43.769
[S03] this non-physical vision, this creative vision,

192
00:11:43.799 --> 00:11:46.259
[S03] can see exactly the building, the house,

193
00:11:46.289 --> 00:11:47.850
[S03] whatever it is that needs to go there

194
00:11:47.879 --> 00:11:49.950
[S03] that would really work well with the curves

195
00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.289
[S03] and the direction of the sun and all that.

196
00:11:53.039 --> 00:11:54.000
[S03] This is a vision.

197
00:11:54.659 --> 00:11:57.600
[S03] Don't all artists say, for example, music composers?

198
00:11:58.139 --> 00:12:01.590
[S03] They say, "I hear it already. I can hear it in my head.

199
00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.590
[S03] All I need to do is to write it down.

200
00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.149
[S03] And once it's written down,

201
00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.500
[S03] all that needs to be done is to be played.

202
00:12:07.529 --> 00:12:09.090
[S03] No imagination necessary."

203
00:12:10.259 --> 00:12:13.590
[S03] And don't writers and all kinds of other artists again say,

204
00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:16.080
[S03] "These words, I feel like they came to me.

205
00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:18.559
[S03] I received them rather than make them up."

206
00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:23.490
[S03] You know this from yourself if you are someone with journals.

207
00:12:23.519 --> 00:12:25.230
[S03] Sometimes you write things and you're like,

208
00:12:25.259 --> 00:12:26.669
[S03] "Wow, did I just write that?

209
00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.399
[S03] Did you go into your imagination

210
00:12:29.429 --> 00:12:31.740
[S03] and try out a different combinations and say,

211
00:12:31.769 --> 00:12:34.230
[S03] "No, that's bad, that's bad, that's bad, that's good."

212
00:12:34.259 --> 00:12:37.049
[S03] And then that's how you came up with that?

213
00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:43.529
[S03] Don't you remember, almost every time, it's just,

214
00:12:43.559 --> 00:12:44.789
[S03] "Wow, I need to write this down."

215
00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.269
[S03] And then afterwards, "Well, I can't believe I wrote this."

216
00:12:48.299 --> 00:12:50.190
[S03] It feels more like a reception

217
00:12:50.909 --> 00:12:54.090
[S03] rather than me having come up with it, me having invented it.

218
00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:58.200
[S03] And it's the same with the painter.

219
00:12:58.230 --> 00:12:59.759
[S03] They say, "I can see it. I can see it.

220
00:12:59.789 --> 00:13:01.559
[S03] I just need to put it down on the canvas."

221
00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:05.429
[S03] That is not imagination.

222
00:13:06.539 --> 00:13:08.700
[S03] That is creative vision.

223
00:13:09.899 --> 00:13:15.330
[S03] And that vision, not only does it not rely on imagination,

224
00:13:15.779 --> 00:13:17.250
[S03] imagination is its enemy.

225
00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:20.759
[S03] That vision cannot be received

226
00:13:21.299 --> 00:13:25.230
[S03] when the seeing is blocked by imaginations.

227
00:13:27.899 --> 00:13:33.029
[S03] All day, we are having dinosaurs fight each other in our heads, still.

228
00:13:34.049 --> 00:13:35.549
[S03] And all day, we are imagining,

229
00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.679
[S03] "What would my life have been like if this?

230
00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.500
[S03] What could it still be like if now I started doing this

231
00:13:40.529 --> 00:13:42.509
[S03] and this and this went this way and then that?"

232
00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:45.899
[S03] All of this is going on.

233
00:13:45.929 --> 00:13:49.049
[S03] And so this vision cannot be received. It is blocked.

234
00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.610
[S03] There's already a movie playing.

235
00:13:50.639 --> 00:13:52.259
[S03] You can't play two movies at once.

236
00:13:54.659 --> 00:13:58.049
[S03] And so if we let go of our imagination,

237
00:13:58.559 --> 00:14:00.000
[S03] this vision can come in.

238
00:14:00.629 --> 00:14:02.909
[S03] And this vision, if you're an artist,

239
00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.950
[S03] will tell you exactly what to draw,

240
00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:07.470
[S03] what to write, what to sculpt, what to make, what to build.

241
00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.990
[S03] If you're a maker, it will tell you exactly how to do it.

242
00:14:11.429 --> 00:14:13.559
[S03] If you have any kind of logistical problems,

243
00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:57.500
[S04] We were just, in that sixteen hours, we were just focusing on it so much that we were open enough.

244
00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:01.899
[S04] Because we're focusing on this, we're open, and we're not allowing the dinosaurs right now.

245
00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:08.580
[S04] We're saying, "I'm looking for this," and so we opened up just a little bit so that the solution could come in, the creative solution.

246
00:15:10.179 --> 00:15:13.100
[S04] And so, it has nothing to do with imagination.

247
00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:16.500
[S04] And this is the law of the universe.

248
00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:21.720
[S04] All that is truly good is wholly good.

249
00:15:23.779 --> 00:15:27.700
[S04] Meaning, all that is really good is entirely good. There's no bad to it.

250
00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:33.100
[S04] This universe never asks you to take in nutrition together with poison.

251
00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:35.679
[S04] And to get the nutrition, you have to eat the poison.

252
00:15:36.639 --> 00:15:38.399
[S04] It has never asked you to do that.

253
00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:45.480
[S04] Every single thing that is truly good, love, truth, justice,

254
00:15:46.639 --> 00:15:49.899
[S04] these are wholly good, entirely good.

255
00:15:52.159 --> 00:15:55.600
[S04] And why should it be any differently with this?

256
00:15:56.509 --> 00:15:58.370
[S04] There's nothing good about imagination.

257
00:15:59.179 --> 00:16:03.320
[S04] At least, not in the spiritual so-called realm, when you're saying,

258
00:16:03.399 --> 00:16:07.740
[S04] "How should I live? What should my life look like? What is the meaning of this life?"

259
00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:13.940
[S04] Then you do not go into imagination. Imagination cannot help you there. Imagination is you, it's your mind.

260
00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:18.679
[S04] The mind cannot perceive these things. There's a reality, there's a truth out there,

261
00:16:18.879 --> 00:16:24.080
[S04] that the mind can have certain insights into, to some degree, sometimes.

262
00:16:24.679 --> 00:16:27.879
[S04] But this mind is never gonna be able to wrap itself around that.

263
00:16:28.919 --> 00:16:33.299
[S04] And the imagination therefore won't be able to either. This truth is speaking to you.

264
00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:38.879
[S04] This truth is trying to come in at once. It cannot wait to come in.

265
00:16:39.399 --> 00:16:44.519
[S04] But we have to, we have to empty ourselves first for that to be able to fill us up.

266
00:16:46.299 --> 00:16:50.279
[S04] And so, I challenge you, this is not a challenge, you will see,

267
00:16:51.179 --> 00:16:54.679
[S04] every time you go into your imagination, stop.

268
00:16:55.159 --> 00:16:58.299
[S04] Just stop for the sake of it, not because you know it's going to work out.

269
00:16:58.799 --> 00:17:04.400
[S04] Fully expect that you're gonna have a terrible experience and fully expect that you wish you had gone into your imagination.

270
00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:07.380
[S04] Fully expect that, and do it anyway.

271
00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:12.799
[S04] Don't allow the imagination. Just as an experiment, be scientific about this.

272
00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:20.470
[S04] "I'm gonna experiment. If this experiment is successful, I'm gonna double down on it. If it's unsuccessful, I'm gonna double down on the imagination."

273
00:17:21.099 --> 00:17:24.880
[S04] Because if imagination is something good, then we should double down, triple down on it.

274
00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:27.400
[S04] Why are we doing this half thing?

275
00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:36.400
[S04] And this is very important for when we do this. Every time we go into our imagination, let us stop ourselves if we can.

276
00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:42.799
[S04] But if we realize, "Oh no, I've been in my imagination for half an hour already and I didn't realize."

277
00:17:43.299 --> 00:17:44.279
[S04] It's not a failure.

278
00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:47.119
[S04] That is not a failure. Let that happen.

279
00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:52.839
[S04] The fact that you're realizing that you were in your imagination for half an hour or ten hours,

280
00:17:53.079 --> 00:17:56.400
[S04] that is a success. It is not a failure.

281
00:17:57.480 --> 00:18:03.000
[S04] Because this machine has been running for so long, it's not just gonna be able to be stopped

282
00:18:03.799 --> 00:18:08.200
[S04] at a moment. Of course, we're gonna keep falling back into it for however long.

283
00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:14.480
[S04] But before we allowed it, now, even if we're two hours into it, we can say,

284
00:18:14.559 --> 00:18:17.400
[S04] "Okay, that happened. I'm gonna come back out of it."

285
00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:23.880
[S04] And as we do that, we're gonna be able to come out sooner and sooner and, and at some point even say,

286
00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.279
[S04] "I'm slipping into the imagination. I haven't even slipped into it yet."

287
00:18:28.079 --> 00:18:34.400
[S04] But I'm, I was just about to escape into it because, again, this person is so boring and they've been going on for a long time and

288
00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:38.599
[S04] I'm at work, I can't just tell them to shut up, like, this is, this needs to happen.

289
00:18:39.599 --> 00:18:41.920
[S04] So, instead of escape, I'm gonna stay right here.

290
00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:43.799
[S04] I'm just gonna do that.

291
00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:50.440
[S04] And I'm telling you that the beauty you're gonna start seeing

292
00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:56.920
[S04] in reality, without escaping it whatsoever, without inventing, imagining, escaping into anything,

293
00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:03.200
[S04] and the value you're gonna see in that, and how much longer your day is gonna become,

294
00:19:04.519 --> 00:19:11.359
[S04] and how much better your sleep is going to be, and how much more likely you're going to be able to get out of bed easier,

295
00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:20.079
[S04] and to find time and energy and attention and focus for all those things that you always wanted to do, always wanted to devote yourself more,

296
00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:23.599
[S04] such as perhaps philosophy, as we do on this channel.

297
00:19:25.799 --> 00:19:31.000
[S04] It's going to be mind-blowing, and I, I can promise you that, if only you give yourself to it.

298
00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:34.509
[S04] This is the one rule: observe.

299
00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:36.079
[S04] Observe.

300
00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:39.390
[S04] Every time you say, you know,

301
00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:45.799
[S04] "It's nice, I'm at the park right now, I'm sitting here with my dog, but she keeps looking at

302
00:19:46.279 --> 00:19:50.200
[S04] ducks and things and she's so nervous. I wish she would be more calm.

303
00:19:50.509 --> 00:19:54.440
[S04] I wish I had a cold drink, it's kind of warm, but I don't wanna get up."

304
00:19:55.059 --> 00:19:57.150
[S05] Every time I catch myself doing that,

305
00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:02.549
[S05] and then the imagination tells me, "Come escape into me.

306
00:20:03.319 --> 00:20:04.430
[S05] It's much better here.

307
00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:07.430
[S05] You can have all the drinks you want here.

308
00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:08.720
[S05] Don't allow it.

309
00:20:09.519 --> 00:20:10.589
[S05] Sit with that.

310
00:20:10.789 --> 00:20:13.119
[S05] Sit with that, say, "But this is reality.

311
00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:16.319
[S05] This is how it is, and it's still beautiful.

312
00:20:16.349 --> 00:20:23.829
[S05] I'm, I'm so lucky to have this dog who's such a beautiful personality.

313
00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:30.269
[S05] And to be able to free, to be free, to be able to do this and to not be stuck in

314
00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:35.269
[S05] some place that doesn't have any natural beauty.

315
00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:37.950
[S05] There's always something to be grateful for,

316
00:20:38.589 --> 00:20:42.069
[S05] and your gratitude is just going to increase, increase, increase as you do this.

317
00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:49.109
[S05] Really, life is so beautiful, and it's not only beautiful for the privileged.

318
00:20:49.309 --> 00:20:55.269
[S05] That's another lie that the imagination tells us, because it doesn't want to let go of us.

319
00:20:56.029 --> 00:20:59.549
[S05] It says, "Others have it well, you will never be able to have it well.

320
00:21:00.109 --> 00:21:04.349
[S05] Uh, maybe one day, maybe one day, if you achieve this and this and this and this,

321
00:21:04.390 --> 00:21:08.589
[S05] perhaps then you can be happy, perhaps then you can be at peace, perhaps then you can,

322
00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:12.940
[S05] you will be able to see some beauty in the world, but until then, there is no beauty you see.

323
00:21:13.349 --> 00:21:14.349
[S05] It's a lie.

324
00:21:15.470 --> 00:21:16.349
[S05] It's a lie.

325
00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:20.029
[S05] Some of the least intelligent people live this way.

326
00:21:20.549 --> 00:21:25.029
[S05] In peace, without imagination, in creativity, in beauty, in truth and in love.

327
00:21:25.349 --> 00:21:27.789
[S05] And some of the poorest people live this way,

328
00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:33.509
[S05] and they do not look at anyone else for solutions, for salvation, they already have it.

329
00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:36.789
[S05] And I ask,

330
00:21:38.029 --> 00:21:39.589
[S05] why shouldn't we be able to do that?
